Task 1: Implement Horizontal Pod Autoscaling
Subtask 1.1: Deploy a Sample Application
First, let's deploy a sample web application that we can scale.

Login to OpenShift cluster:
oc login --server=https://your-openshift-cluster:6443 --username=developer --password=developer
Create a new project:
oc new-project scaling-lab
Deploy a sample PHP application:
oc new-app php:8.0~https://github.com/sclorg/cakephp-ex.git --name=cakephp-app
Wait for the build to complete:
oc get builds -w
Expose the application:
oc expose svc/cakephp-app
Verify the deployment:
oc get pods
oc get routes
Subtask 1.2: Configure Resource Requests and Limits
Before implementing autoscaling, we need to set resource requests and limits.

Create a resource configuration file:
cat > app-resources.yaml << EOF
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: cakephp-app
spec:
  template:
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: cakephp-app
        resources:
          requests:
            cpu: 100m
            memory: 128Mi
          limits:
            cpu: 500m
            memory: 512Mi
EOF
Apply the resource configuration:
oc patch deployment cakephp-app --patch-file app-resources.yaml
Verify the resource configuration:
oc describe deployment cakephp-app | grep -A 10 "Limits\|Requests"
Subtask 1.3: Create Horizontal Pod Autoscaler
Create HPA configuration file:
cat > hpa-config.yaml << EOF
apiVersion: autoscaling/v2
kind: HorizontalPodAutoscaler
metadata:
  name: cakephp-app-hpa
  namespace: scaling-lab
spec:
  scaleTargetRef:
    apiVersion: apps/v1
    kind: Deployment
    name: cakephp-app
  minReplicas: 2
  maxReplicas: 10
  metrics:
  - type: Resource
    resource:
      name: cpu
      target:
        type: Utilization
        averageUtilization: 70
  - type: Resource
    resource:
      name: memory
      target:
        type: Utilization
        averageUtilization: 80
EOF
Apply the HPA configuration:
oc apply -f hpa-config.yaml
Verify HPA creation:
oc get hpa
oc describe hpa cakephp-app-hpa
Subtask 1.4: Test Autoscaling Behavior
Monitor current pod count:
oc get pods -l deployment=cakephp-app
Generate load to trigger scaling:
# Get the application route
APP_ROUTE=$(oc get route cakephp-app -o jsonpath='{.spec.host}')

# Generate load using a load testing pod
oc run load-generator --image=busybox --restart=Never -- /bin/sh -c "while true; do wget -q -O- http://$APP_ROUTE; done"
Monitor scaling in real-time:
# In one terminal, watch HPA status
watch oc get hpa

# In another terminal, watch pod scaling
watch oc get pods -l deployment=cakephp-app
Check HPA events:
oc describe hpa cakephp-app-hpa
Clean up load generator:
oc delete pod load-generator
Task 2: Set Up Readiness and Liveness Probes
Subtask 2.1: Configure Liveness Probe
Liveness probes determine if a container is running properly and restart it if needed.

Create liveness probe configuration:
cat > liveness-probe.yaml << EOF
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: cakephp-app
spec:
  template:
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: cakephp-app
        livenessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /
            port: 8080
            scheme: HTTP
          initialDelaySeconds: 30
          periodSeconds: 10
          timeoutSeconds: 5
          failureThreshold: 3
          successThreshold: 1
EOF
Apply the liveness probe:
oc patch deployment cakephp-app --patch-file liveness-probe.yaml
Verify the probe configuration:
oc describe deployment cakephp-app | grep -A 10 "Liveness"
Subtask 2.2: Configure Readiness Probe
Readiness probes determine if a container is ready to receive traffic.

Create readiness probe configuration:
cat > readiness-probe.yaml << EOF
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: cakephp-app
spec:
  template:
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: cakephp-app
        readinessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /
            port: 8080
            scheme: HTTP
          initialDelaySeconds: 5
          periodSeconds: 5
          timeoutSeconds: 3
          failureThreshold: 3
          successThreshold: 1
EOF
Apply the readiness probe:
oc patch deployment cakephp-app --patch-file readiness-probe.yaml
Verify both probes are configured:
oc describe deployment cakephp-app | grep -A 15 "Liveness\|Readiness"
Subtask 2.3: Create a Combined Health Check Configuration
Create a comprehensive health check configuration:
cat > health-checks.yaml << EOF
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: cakephp-app
  namespace: scaling-lab
spec:
  template:
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: cakephp-app
        resources:
          requests:
            cpu: 100m
            memory: 128Mi
          limits:
            cpu: 500m
            memory: 512Mi
        livenessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /
            port: 8080
            scheme: HTTP
          initialDelaySeconds: 30
          periodSeconds: 10
          timeoutSeconds: 5
          failureThreshold: 3
          successThreshold: 1
        readinessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /
            port: 8080
            scheme: HTTP
          initialDelaySeconds: 5
          periodSeconds: 5
          timeoutSeconds: 3
          failureThreshold: 3
          successThreshold: 1
        startupProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /
            port: 8080
            scheme: HTTP
          initialDelaySeconds: 10
          periodSeconds: 10
          timeoutSeconds: 5
          failureThreshold: 30
          successThreshold: 1
EOF
Apply the complete configuration:
oc apply -f health-checks.yaml
Monitor pod health status:
oc get pods -w
Subtask 2.4: Test Health Check Behavior
Simulate application failure:
# Get a pod name
POD_NAME=$(oc get pods -l deployment=cakephp-app -o jsonpath='{.items[0].metadata.name}')

# Simulate failure by stopping the web server process
oc exec $POD_NAME -- pkill -f httpd
Monitor pod restart behavior:
oc get pods -w
oc describe pod $POD_NAME
Check events for health check failures:
oc get events --sort-by='.lastTimestamp' | grep -i probe
Task 3: Scale Applications Manually and Automatically
Subtask 3.1: Manual Scaling Operations
Scale up manually using CLI:
oc scale deployment cakephp-app --replicas=5
Verify scaling:
oc get pods -l deployment=cakephp-app
Scale down manually:
oc scale deployment cakephp-app --replicas=2
Scale using the web console:
Open OpenShift web console in your browser
Navigate to your project: scaling-lab
Go to Workloads > Deployments
Click on cakephp-app deployment
Use the scale up/down arrows or edit the replica count
Subtask 3.2: Configure Advanced Autoscaling
Create advanced HPA with multiple metrics:
cat > advanced-hpa.yaml << EOF
apiVersion: autoscaling/v2
kind: HorizontalPodAutoscaler
metadata:
  name: cakephp-app-advanced-hpa
  namespace: scaling-lab
spec:
  scaleTargetRef:
    apiVersion: apps/v1
    kind: Deployment
    name: cakephp-app
  minReplicas: 2
  maxReplicas: 15
  metrics:
  - type: Resource
    resource:
      name: cpu
      target:
        type: Utilization
        averageUtilization: 60
  - type: Resource
    resource:
      name: memory
      target:
        type: Utilization
        averageUtilization: 70
  behavior:
    scaleUp:
      stabilizationWindowSeconds: 60
      policies:
      - type: Percent
        value: 100
        periodSeconds: 60
      - type: Pods
        value: 2
        periodSeconds: 60
    scaleDown:
      stabilizationWindowSeconds: 300
      policies:
      - type: Percent
        value: 50
        periodSeconds: 60
EOF
Replace the existing HPA:
oc delete hpa cakephp-app-hpa
oc apply -f advanced-hpa.yaml
Monitor the new HPA:
oc get hpa cakephp-app-advanced-hpa -w
Subtask 3.3: Load Testing and Monitoring
Create a more sophisticated load test:
cat > load-test.yaml << EOF
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: load-test
  namespace: scaling-lab
spec:
  containers:
  - name: load-test
    image: busybox
    command:
    - /bin/sh
    - -c
    - |
      APP_ROUTE="http://cakephp-app:8080"
      echo "Starting load test against \$APP_ROUTE"
      for i in \$(seq 1 1000); do
        for j in \$(seq 1 10); do
          wget -q -O- \$APP_ROUTE &
        done
        sleep 1
        echo "Completed batch \$i"
      done
      echo "Load test completed"
  restartPolicy: Never
EOF
Run the load test:
oc apply -f load-test.yaml
Monitor scaling behavior:
# Terminal 1: Watch HPA
watch oc get hpa

# Terminal 2: Watch pods
watch oc get pods

# Terminal 3: Monitor resource usage
oc top pods
Check load test progress:
oc logs load-test -f
Subtask 3.4: Vertical Pod Autoscaling (VPA) Setup
Create VPA configuration:
cat > vpa-config.yaml << EOF
apiVersion: autoscaling.k8s.io/v1
kind: VerticalPodAutoscaler
metadata:
  name: cakephp-app-vpa
  namespace: scaling-lab
spec:
  targetRef:
    apiVersion: apps/v1
    kind: Deployment
    name: cakephp-app
  updatePolicy:
    updateMode: "Auto"
  resourcePolicy:
    containerPolicies:
    - containerName: cakephp-app
      maxAllowed:
        cpu: 1
        memory: 1Gi
      minAllowed:
        cpu: 50m
        memory: 64Mi
EOF
Apply VPA configuration (Note: VPA may not be available in all clusters):
oc apply -f vpa-config.yaml || echo "VPA not available in this cluster"
Monitoring and Troubleshooting
Common Issues and Solutions
HPA not scaling:
# Check metrics server
oc get apiservice v1beta1.metrics.k8s.io -o yaml

# Check resource requests are set
oc describe deployment cakephp-app | grep -A 5 "Requests"

# Check HPA status
oc describe hpa cakephp-app-advanced-hpa
Pods failing health checks:
# Check pod events
oc describe pod <pod-name>

# Check application logs
oc logs <pod-name>

# Test health check endpoint manually
oc port-forward <pod-name> 8080:8080
curl http://localhost:8080/
Resource constraints:
# Check node resources
oc describe nodes

# Check resource quotas
oc describe quota

# Check limit ranges
oc describe limitrange
Monitoring Commands
Real-time monitoring:
# Watch all resources
watch oc get pods,hpa,deployment

# Monitor resource usage
watch oc top pods

# Check cluster events
oc get events --sort-by='.lastTimestamp'
Performance metrics:
# Get detailed pod metrics
oc adm top pods --containers

# Get node metrics
oc adm top nodes
Cleanup
Remove load test resources:
oc delete pod load-test
oc delete pod load-generator --ignore-not-found=true
Clean up HPA and VPA:
oc delete hpa cakephp-app-advanced-hpa
oc delete vpa cakephp-app-vpa --ignore-not-found=true
Optional: Delete the entire project:
oc delete project scaling-lab
